{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017GXA6kDA7PLyZPRfFmYX55","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Checklist for `true-bdd us apply <story-id>`.\n2\t# Walk every AC in the refined story and merge each one into the registry\n3\t# (docs/scenarios.yaml).\n4\t#\n5\t# Engine-test prompt set: intentionally minimal (2 prompts) to exercise the\n6\t# many-scenarios × many-prompts walk and the per-cell fix loop. Will be\n7\t# expanded with richer merge-correctness checks once the engine is proven.\n8\t\n9\tversion: \"1.0\"\n10\tlast_updated: \"2026-04-25\"\n11\t\n12\t# Per-checklist engine knob, read by `us apply --fix` to bound the outer\n13\t# re-walk loop: any fix applied during walk N re-walks from AC 1 prompt 1;\n14\t# N reaching max_apply_attempts without a clean walk aborts, registry untouched.\n15\tconfig:\n16\t  max_apply_attempts: 5\n17\t\n18\tsections:\n19\t  - id: merge\n20\t    name: \"Scenario Merge\"\n21\t    description: \"Each AC from the story must be present, and only once, in the registry.\"\n22\t    validation_prompts:\n23\t      - Q: |\n24\t          Does this acceptance criterion already appear as a scenario in the\n25\t          registry?\n26\t\n27\t          The registry is the requirements YAML referenced by the subject\n28\t          (the scratch copy for this run). An AC \"appears\" when there is an\n29\t          entry under `scenarios:` whose `user_stories[]` list contains the\n30\t          subject's story path AND the subject's lineage scenario id.\n31\t\n32\t          Pass when at least one such entry exists.\n33\t          Fail otherwise.\n34\t\n35\t          Context: emit one line.\n36\t            - \"AC <ac id> (lineage <lineage id>): present in <matched scenario id>\"\n37\t            - \"AC <ac id> (lineage <lineage id>): not present\"\n38\t        rationale: \"Every refined-story AC must be reflected as a tracked scenario in the registry.\"\n39\t        F: |\n40\t          Add this AC as a new scenario in the registry.\n41\t\n42\t          Use the Edit tool against the registry file referenced by the\n43\t          subject. Steps:\n44\t            1. Pick the next free id following existing numbering — `INT-NNN`\n45\t               for integration-layer ACs, `E2E-NNN` for e2e-layer ACs. If\n46\t               unsure, prefer `E2E-NNN`. Do not reuse an existing id.\n47\t            2. Insert a new entry under `scenarios:` with:\n48\t                  description: <short summary derived from the AC description>\n49\t                  service: \"\"\n50\t                  path: <see below>\n51\t                  last_updated: \"<today, YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n52\t                  user_stories:\n53\t                    - story: <story file path from subject>\n54\t                      scenario_id: <lineage id from subject>\n55\t                      merge_date: \"<today, YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n56\t                  merged_steps:\n57\t                    given: <verbatim from the AC's steps.given>\n58\t                    when:  <verbatim from the AC's steps.when>\n59\t                    then:  <verbatim from the AC's steps.then>\n60\t            3. `path:` names the generated test file this scenario's Go\n61\t               test is written into. REUSE an existing `path:` from a\n62\t               scenario of the same command or feature family — several\n63\t               scenarios share one file on purpose, so related\n64\t               behaviours are read together. Invent a new one only when\n65\t               no existing file fits, and then make it\n66\t               `<suite path>/<family>_test.go`, where <suite path> is\n67\t               the `path:` of the architecture.testing.suites[] entry\n68\t               whose `service:` matches this scenario's.\n69\t            4. Preserve existing file ordering and indentation. Do not\n70\t               touch any other entry.\n71\t\n72\t      - Q: |\n73\t          Does the registry contain duplicate entries for this acceptance\n